        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): bound embedding batch file upload error body read",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`response.text()` in the Gemini batch file upload error path read the\nresponse body unbounded into memory and embedded it in the Error message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced manual `response.ok` check + `response.text()` + `throw Error`\nwith `assertOkOrThrowProviderError`, which provides bounded reads, redaction,\nand structured `ProviderHttpError` metadata — following #102953 (steipete).\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** unbounded `response.text()` + raw body in error message\n**After:** bounded via `assertOkOrThrowProviderError` with redacted metadata\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Targeted path proof (Gemini file upload via assertOkOrThrowProviderError)\n\nReal HTTP 400 with sensitive Google API error body → `assertOkOrThrowProviderError(response, \"gemini.batch-file-upload\")`:\n\n```\n=== #103306 Proof: assertOkOrThrowProviderError on Gemini file upload path ===\nError thrown: PASS\nProviderHttpError instance: PASS\nError name ProviderHttpError: PASS\nStatus 400: PASS\nLabel \"gemini.batch-file-upload\": PASS\nAPI_KEY_INVALID not leaked: PASS\nService domain not leaked: PASS\nRaw JSON not leaked: PASS\nStructured code INVALID_ARGUMENT: PASS\n\nMessage: gemini.batch-file-upload (400): The API key included in the request is invalid. [code=INVALID_ARGUMENT]\nCode: INVALID_ARGUMENT\nStatus: 400\n\nOverall: ALL PASS\n```\n\n### Tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google/embedding-batch.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n```\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nextensions/google/embedding-batch.ts | 6 ++-- (assertOkOrThrowProviderError)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
        "branch": "fix/google-embedding-error-body-file",
